  "learnSubtitle": "A clear look at BCI, EEG, and the limits of the technology.",
  "lesson1Title": "Neurons and EEG",
  "lesson2Title": "What is a BCI?",
  "lesson3Title": "Invasive vs non-invasive",
  "lesson4Title": "Ultrasound, magnetism, light",
  "lesson5Title": "Can Wi-Fi read the brain?",
  "lesson6Title": "Ethics and privacy",
  "lesson1Body": "Neurons talk in tiny electrical pulses. EEG listens from the scalp, picking up the summed activity of millions of neurons at once \u2014 a blurry, noisy window, never a single thought.",
  "lesson2Body": "A brain\u2013computer interface turns brain signals into commands or feedback: signal, decode, respond. Nemro\u2019s loop is exactly that \u2014 and it is only as good as the signal it reads.",
  "lesson3Body": "Implanted electrodes hear single neurons clearly, but need surgery. Scalp EEG is safe and easy, but coarse and noisy. Nemro stays on the non-invasive side \u2014 and Live uses no EEG at all, only a camera proxy.",
  "lesson4Body": "Ultrasound, MEG, and near-infrared light each sense the brain differently, trading precision for cost and portability. None of them reads thoughts either \u2014 they all measure indirect, noisy signals.",
  "lesson5Body": "No. Wi-Fi sensing notices movement and posture from disturbed radio waves \u2014 it never touches brain activity. Any product claiming to read your mind over Wi-Fi is hype, or a scam.",
  "lesson6Body": "Brain data is intimate, even when it is noisy. Nemro keeps everything on this device: no accounts, no tracking, no uploads. Session history is opt-in, and you can delete it any time.",
