  "privacyDataTitle": "What data is stored?",
  "privacyDataBody": "Language, theme, onboarding state, camera lens preference, and an optional camera baseline range. Live session summaries are saved on this device only if you turn saving on in Settings, and deleting all data in Settings wipes them. The Lab decoder processes the bundled sample locally; no EEG is collected from you.",
  "privacyDecoderTitle": "On-device AI",
  "privacyDecoderBody": "The Lab decoder is a small model bundled with the app. It runs locally on the EEG sample, and predictions never leave the device.",
  "privacyCameraTitle": "Camera",
  "privacyCameraBody": "Live opens the camera only after you tap Start. Frames are downsampled and processed on-device to estimate a rough light/contrast/motion proxy. No video or images are recorded, stored, or uploaded. An optional calibration baseline (two numbers) can be stored locally. The camera is released when you stop or leave the app; Nemro does not request microphone or storage access.",
